{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr55oDii63hEbW3LfVkw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the code that deletes the sessions, so this diagnosis is a best guess. The retrieved snippets only show lines 515–520 of `AuthService.update` and not the password-change block above them.\n\nThe symptoms point to the wrong ID being passed as the session to keep. The current session is deleted, and an unrelated older session survives, probably one whose ID happens to equal the user's ID. In the upstream nestjs-boilerplate this block calls `sessionService.deleteByUserIdWithExclude({ userId, excludeId })`. I suspect `excludeId` is not `userJwtPayload.sessionId`. It may be `userJwtPayload.id` (the user ID), or the type may be wrong. The second candidate is the session delete itself, in case the exclusion filter is wrong there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1090d06e-2209-47fe-b8ca-b44b9b36ab53","uuid":"5adef8c9-4ed2-4231-b131-db1fc97d95d7","timestamp":"2026-11-08T20:12:38.820Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr55nyaHzf7CBrgiW5qL"}
